# Git safety

## Commit author

AI commits must use:

```
Sisyphus <sisyphus@codelint.dev>
```

```bash
git commit --author="Sisyphus <sisyphus@codelint.dev>" -m "type: description"
```

## Hooks

After clone (or in Cursor Cloud `install`), run:

```bash
./setup.sh
```

This sets an absolute `core.hooksPath` to `.githooks`.

Never use `--no-verify` unless the user explicitly asks.

### pre-commit

- clang-format on staged C++ (auto-fix)
- trailing whitespace / newlines
- sensitive file detection

### commit-msg

- format: `type: description` (or `type(scope): description`)
- blocks commits on `main` / `master` / `production` / `release`
